# Fixed defect 130, 2026-09-28, beside it: a thesis rule is not a failure.
# Symptom: a statement whose only report was one of the rules the thesis adds
# (`diag.is_thesis_rule`) was recovered from as if it had failed, so the line
# after a `match` holding `0 => x = 5` was dropped, and so was the `)` left
# after a list that `spaced_minus_element` refused; and `check --permissive`,
# which drops the thesis rules, then said nothing at all about either program
# and passed it on, exit 0 over a line that does not parse. Cause: the
# recovery asked whether any diagnostic had been said. It asks whether a
# refusal was (`cursor.refused_since`): a thesis rule leaves the program a
# meaning, and nothing is dropped on its account.

function after_an_arm(n: i64)
    match n
        0 => x = 5  #~ declaration_in_arm
        _ => print(2)
    z = 4 )  #~ expected_end_of_line

function after_a_list(a: i64, b: i64)
    xs = [a
        - b] )  #~ spaced_minus_element #~ expected_end_of_line
    print(xs.len())

function main()
    print(1)
